# provenance_reserved.tkr — the D133 provenance REJECT host. A user unit under src/ redefines the
# reserved base type `str`; the injected base prelude alone owns the reserved names, so the build
# fails with the reserved-name diagnostic. It has no successful build to sanitize/run.

Feature: provenance reserved-name — the compiler rejects a user redefinition of a reserved base type

  Scenario: redef_str — a user unit declares `type str`
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "type 'str' is reserved"
